      rationale: "Confusion, eye movement abnormalities, and ataxia make up the classic triad of [[wernicke-encephalopathy|Wernicke encephalopathy]]. Here the cause is not alcohol but bariatric surgery with weeks of vomiting, a setting Sechi and Serra and the EFNS guideline both highlight. The CT is expected to be normal. Parenteral thiamine is given immediately, without waiting for a level or MRI.",
